# Pins of the owner's tools (scripts/multichain/owner-toolchain.sh; review finding R369-16).
#
# Every value below was taken on 2026-11-17 from the publisher's own release artefact, downloaded over HTTPS from
# the URL on the same line, and compared with the checksum the publisher publishes:
#
# Foundry v1.7.1 (release of 2026-05-08, https://github.com/foundry-rs/foundry/releases/tag/v1.7.1, marked
#   immutable by GitHub): the archive hashes equal the release's own `foundry_v1.7.1_darwin_<arch>.sha256` files and
#   the asset digests of the GitHub release API. The release also carries a Sigstore bundle per archive
#   (`.sigstore.json`) and a GitHub attestation (darwin_amd64: https://github.com/foundry-rs/foundry/attestations/26853710,
#   darwin_arm64: .../26853990); those signatures were NOT verified when these pins were written (no verifier was
#   available to the agent), only the published checksums.
# Node.js v24.21.0 (https://nodejs.org/dist/v24.21.0/): the archive hashes equal the lines of the release's
#   SHASUMS256.txt (itself SHA-256 f410428039e2c922a14058df067a4482691c9304a5c01a75847f9f3f2d3307f6). The PGP
#   signature of that file (SHASUMS256.txt.asc) was NOT verified when these pins were written.
# libusb 1.0.30 (Intel Macs only): Foundry's Intel build loads `libusb-1.0.0.dylib` from a Homebrew path. The
#   archive is Homebrew's own bottle for x86_64 macOS ("sonoma": built for macOS 14 or later), whose SHA-256 is the
#   one Homebrew publishes at https://formulae.brew.sh/api/formula/libusb.json (and is the blob's own address at
#   ghcr.io). The Apple-silicon build of Foundry v1.7.1 does not load libusb.
#
# Lines: <platform> <kind> <sha256 or -> <name> [<url or text>]
#   archive: a release archive, checked before it is unpacked.   member: the one file taken from the libusb bottle.
#   file:    a program inside the tools directory, checked by name at every check.
#   tree:    the digest of the whole tools directory as owner-toolchain.sh builds it (every file, link, executable bit
#            and directory), from two independent installs that agreed.
#   version: the first line `<name> --version` must print ("_" stands for a space).
#
# To change a pin: download the publisher's artefact yourself, compare it with the publisher's checksum, and have a
# reviewer repeat it. Never copy a hash from an installed copy.

